<urn:atm:triage:finding/AY14-QA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AY14-QA-002" ;
  triage:title "From<&AgentName> for HerdrAgentName panics via .expect() on out-of-grammar canonical names at three production call sites; pre-existing roster rows never re-validated" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr qa-pr1305-r1 (PR #1305, AY.14 herdr-agent-name-mapping, head 23cebc85f). Cross-confirmed by rust-best-practices-agent RBP-F001 (Critical) and rust-qa-agent QA-001 (Important). impl From<&AgentName> for HerdrAgentName at crates/atm-core/src/delivery_channel.rs:76-78 asserts infallibility with .expect(), but the AgentName grammar (validate_path_segment: mixed case, unbounded length) is not a subset of the Herdr grammar ^[a-z][a-z0-9_-]{0,31}$. Production call sites with no fallible fallback: crates/atm-core/src/send/hook.rs:59 (sync post-send hot path), crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs:775 (periodic wake loop over every herdr-backend roster row), crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/replacement_handler.rs:160 (doctor probe). The CLI write-time gate validates only freshly created or updated herdr-backend members; nothing re-validates pre-existing rows or gates the read paths, so any out-of-grammar canonical name on a herdr-backend member panics the wake loop on every poll, contradicting AC1 (members without alias behave exactly as before). Required correction: replace the From impl with a fallible TryFrom / Result conversion, apply the existing skip-and-log policy for invalid herdrAgent values at all three call sites, collapse the duplicated absent-alias fallback (RBQA-AY14-F002, herdr_queue_wake.rs:775 and replacement_handler.rs:158-160) into one owner in atm-core delivery_channel, and add a regression test that drives a non-conforming canonical name through each path." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ay" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "runtime-safety" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-core/src/delivery_channel.rs, crates/atm-core/src/send/hook.rs, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs, crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/replacement_handler.rs, every HerdrAgentName::from(&AgentName) call site" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-07T18:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AY14 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-07T18:12:56Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-07T19:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "qa-pr1305-r2 (PR #1305, head 109fdad1e). Fixed under AY14-FIX-R1: panicking From<&AgentName> impl removed from delivery_channel.rs; replaced by fallible resolve_herdr_agent_target (single owner, skip-and-log policy) consumed at all three cited production call sites (send/hook.rs:93, herdr_queue_wake.rs:777, replacement_handler.rs:156). This also closes RBQA-AY14-F002's duplicated fallback logic -- ruthless-boundary-qa confirmed one owner across all three sites, no local re-implementation remains. Regression tests added at delivery_channel.rs, send/tests.rs, herdr_queue_wake.rs, and replacement_handler.rs driving a non-conforming canonical name through each path. rust-qa-agent confirmed fmt/clippy/tests green (cargo test -p atm-core -p atm -p atm-herdr -p atm-http-runtime --all-features, 24/24 ok) and CI Test (windows-latest) on head 109fdad1e passed (run 34153691392), independently confirming the Windows-only compile break in crates/atm-herdr/tests/windows_transport_cli.rs is also resolved. arch-qa PASS, no new boundary violation; HerdrAgentName correctly placed in atm-core (not atm-herdr) to avoid a forbidden atm-core->atm-herdr edge." ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AY14-QA-002/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AY14-QA-002/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AY14-QA-002/3> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AY14-QA-002/4> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

